<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21965" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">implōrātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inpl-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				beseeching for help</i>, <i>imploring</i> (rare
			but good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium deorum et hominum et civium et sociorum
					imploratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 47, 196</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acerba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 5, 63, § 163</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad invidiosam implorationem converti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 2, 38</span></i>
			.</div>
